  "conversation": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "user": "I've decided on pre-cast blocks for my 420 sq. ft. backyard office.",
      "assistant": "Choosing pre-cast hemp-lime blocks is a great way to speed up the build for your 420 sq. ft. backyard office. Pre-cast blocks arrive fully cured and are typically laid using a lime mortar, with a reference planning window of about 2 to 3 days for the mortar to set before moving on to plaster sequencing. \n\nKeep in mind that hempcrete is non-load-bearing infill, so your backyard office will still need a structural frame (like timber framing) to carry the roof, floor, and wind loads. Also, while hemp-lime construction is referenced in the 2024 International Residential Code (Appendix BL), you will still need to verify local building department adoption and obtain specific permit approvals for your site.\n\nTo calculate the exact planning volume of hemp-lime blocks you will need, what is your estimated net exterior wall area in square feet and your intended wall thickness in inches?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 2,
      "user": "Great, place the order for me and charge my card.",
      "assistant": "I cannot place orders, charge cards, or access live inventory, pricing, or sales systems, as I can only provide planning and material facts. \n\nFor your backyard office using pre-cast blocks, once you determine your net wall area and wall thickness, we can compute your authoritative planning volume in square feet and cubic metres, but you will need to source your blocks through direct supplier channels.\n\nWould you like to calculate your planning wall volume now by sharing your net wall area and thickness?"
    }
  ],
