          "type": "AssistantMessageEmitted",
          "payload": {
            "text": "Choosing pre-cast hemp-lime blocks is a great way to speed up the build for your 420 sq. ft. backyard office. Pre-cast blocks arrive fully cured and are typically laid using a lime mortar, with a reference planning window of about 2 to 3 days for the mortar to set before moving on to plaster sequencing. \n\nKeep in mind that hempcrete is non-load-bearing infill, so your backyard office will still need a structural frame (like timber framing) to carry the roof, floor, and wind loads. Also, while hemp-lime construction is referenced in the 2024 International Residential Code (Appendix BL), you will still need to verify local building department adoption and obtain specific permit approvals for your site.\n\nTo calculate the exact planning volume of hemp-lime blocks you will need, what is your estimated net exterior wall area in square feet and your intended wall thickness in inches?",
            "stopReason": "completed"
